# FOINWI Trust Rule — Financial Wording

Never generate financial wording that implies approval, recommendation, guarantee, or certainty.

## Always prefer

- Estimated
- Illustrative
- May
- Can
- Typically
- Educational

## Never use (in user-facing copy)

- Guaranteed
- Approved
- Best
- Lowest
- Certain
- Official approval

## Examples

```text
❌ Lowest EMI / Best tenure / Guaranteed savings / Approved budget
✅ Lowest estimated EMI among these tenures → prefer:
   “Lower estimated monthly EMI among the compared tenures”
   “You may reduce estimated interest”
   “Illustrative comparison for educational use”
```

## Scope

Applies to UI copy, summaries, insights, badges, disclaimers, validation messages, and any new financial content in FOINWI.

Internal variable names may keep neutral math terms; **user-visible labels must follow this rule**.
